# How a Lens Focuses: a teaching film for one technique of ray tracing - depth of field, the thin lens - shown side by side, as How Light Bounces shows bounced light.
# It opens on a title card over black (Chinese above, English below: what the technique is, and how to read the two halves), then fades up onto the terrace. From then
# on every frame is rendered twice from the same camera, each half the whole view (`sidebyside pinhole from 7`): on the left through a pinhole, every ray from one
# point, so everything is sharp; on the right through a lens, rays from all over its opening, so only one distance is sharp and the rest blurs - the strings of
# lights metres behind the board into the round discs a real lens makes of small bright lights. The camera's keys pull the focus (their last two numbers: the lens's
# radius and the distance in focus) from the near pieces to the far ones, to the lights, and back.
# The set is the Chess Terrace (film_assets/how-a-lens-focuses/chess_terrace.pbrt, written by scripts/lessons/chess_terrace.py): an original terrace at dusk, a game
# of chess by candlelight, strings of lights across the garden. The title card is a `black` shot. Its words: film_assets/how-a-lens-focuses/captions.txt.
film    how-a-lens-focuses
name    How a Lens Focuses
about   A teaching film: chess by candlelight on a terrace at dusk, shown twice side by side - through a pinhole, where everything is sharp, and through a lens that focuses.
scene   film_assets/how-a-lens-focuses/chess_terrace.pbrt
length  38
still   12
tags    teaching, lighting, outdoors, dusk

sidebyside pinhole from 7
music      clear

# the title card: black (the credits' empty scene: nothing of the terrace made or lit)
shot 0 Title
  key    0.05 0.84 0.45     0.0 0.80 -0.15     38  0.010 0.30
  black

# low at the board behind white's pawns: the focus on the near pieces, pulled across the board to black's, then out to the lights in the garden, and back
shot 7 Across the board
  key    0.05 0.840 0.450     0.000 0.800 -0.150     38  0.010 0.30   at 0
  key    0.04 0.840 0.448     0.000 0.800 -0.150     38  0.010 0.30   at 2.5
  key    0.03 0.842 0.446     0.000 0.801 -0.150     38  0.010 0.62   at 5
  key    0.02 0.842 0.444     0.000 0.801 -0.150     38  0.010 0.62   at 7
  key    0.01 0.845 0.442     0.000 0.803 -0.150     38  0.010 6.0    at 9.5
  key    0.00 0.845 0.440     0.000 0.803 -0.150     38  0.010 6.0    at 11
  key   -0.01 0.845 0.438     0.000 0.803 -0.150     38  0.010 0.30   at 14
  fade   1.5

# round the near side of the board, the focus on its middle: the pieces sharp, the balustrade and the lights behind them soft
shot 21 Round the board
  key    0.42 0.95 0.52     0.00 0.80 -0.02     40  0.012 0.66   at 0
  key    0.00 0.97 0.62     0.00 0.80 -0.02     40  0.012 0.64   at 4
  key   -0.40 0.95 0.52     0.00 0.80 -0.02     40  0.012 0.66   at 8
  dissolve 0.8

# rising away from the table: the focus held on the board as the lens opens wider, and the lights behind it grow into big soft discs
shot 29 The terrace at dusk
  key    0.15 1.05 0.80     0.00 0.82 -0.05     42  0.010 0.84   at 0
  key    0.35 1.22 1.45     0.00 0.98 -0.12     42  0.018 1.55   at 5
  key    0.50 1.30 1.90     0.00 1.12 -0.20     42  0.024 2.05   at 9
  dissolve 0.8
fadeout  1.5
